Subject: [PATCH] mtd: nand: am335x: report configured page size in SPL

The legacy AM335x SPL NAND reader does not run nand_scan(), so the
private mtd_info writesize remains zero. spl_nand_read() uses
nand_page_size() to set its block length after reading the image header.
A zero block length causes the generic SPL loader's aligned payload read
to fail even when U-Boot was written at the correct NAND offset.

This driver already uses CONFIG_SYS_NAND_PAGE_SIZE for all page reads;
return the same configured size to the generic SPL loader.

---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/am335x_spl_bch.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/am335x_spl_bch.c
@@ -219,6 +219,6 @@
 unsigned int nand_page_size(void)
 {
-	return nand_to_mtd(&nand_chip)->writesize;
+	return CONFIG_SYS_NAND_PAGE_SIZE;
 }
 
 /* Unselect after operation */
